// ============================================================================
// Detection: hostPath Volume Mount (Container Breakout Vector)
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1611 - Escape to Host
// Source: AKSAuditAdmin
// ============================================================================

// HOW THIS DETECTION WORKS
// -------------------------
// A `hostPath` volume mounts a directory from the NODE's filesystem into the pod.
// Mount something sensitive (/ , /var/run/docker.sock, /etc/kubernetes) and the
// container has a window onto the host — the classic container-breakout primitive
// (T1611 Escape to Host). This detection fires at ADMISSION time, when the pod is
// created, so you catch it before the workload even runs.
//
// The interesting mechanic is mv-apply: a pod can declare MANY volumes, so we need
// to inspect the spec.volumes ARRAY element-by-element and keep only the pods that
// have at least one hostPath entry — reporting exactly which volume and host path.
//
// TABLE: AKSAuditAdmin — write/mutating audit events (pod `create` lands here).

AKSAuditAdmin
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)                                  // recent window first
| where Verb == "create" and ObjectRef.resource == "pods"       // only pod-creation events
// mv-apply expands the spec.volumes array into one virtual row per volume, runs
// the inner pipeline on each, and keeps only rows that survive it. The inner
// `where isnotempty(volume.hostPath)` drops every non-hostPath volume, so a pod
// with zero hostPath volumes produces no rows (and drops out of the results).
| mv-apply volume = RequestObject.spec.volumes on (
    where isnotempty(volume.hostPath)                                          // keep hostPath volumes only
    | project VolumeName = tostring(volume.name), HostPath = tostring(volume.hostPath.path)  // surface the volume + host dir
  )
// Tune: CSI node drivers / monitoring agents legitimately mount hostPath in
// kube-system — allowlist those, alert on hostPath in workload namespaces.
| where User.username != "aksService" and User.username !startswith "system:"  // drop AKS + control-plane creators
| project TimeGenerated, User = tostring(User.username), ClientIp = tostring(SourceIps[0]),   // who + from where
          Namespace = tostring(ObjectRef.namespace), Pod = tostring(ObjectRef.name),           // which pod
          VolumeName, HostPath, RequestUri                                                     // and exactly what it mounted
| extend MitreTechnique = "T1611"    // tag with the ATT&CK technique
